<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<CustomField xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        THIS COMMENT SITS INSIDE THE ROOT ELEMENT DELIBERATELY. A comment placed ABOVE
        <CustomField> breaks `sf` deploy at source conversion with a misleading "unable to find
        matching parent xml file" error.

        ADDED 2026-08-21 (buyer-to-broker-counterparty-change.md). REPLACES Buyer__c AS THE NDA
        COUNTERPARTY ON THE DISPOSITION SIDE, BY EXPLICIT USER DECISION: "we don't need buyer
        information, we just need broker contact for disposition offers and NDA" / "everything
        must be linked with broker contact as he is the only person that DPEG will be
        communicating." DPEG communicates only with the appointed listing broker on the sale -
        one per disposition, not one per interested buyer - so this lookup targets
        Disposition__c.Broker__c's population (the Contact.Broker record type), not a
        deal-scoped buyer principal. Role-named Contact lookup, explicitly permitted by
        ARCHITECTURE.md §1.

        =====================================================================================
        XML SHAPE IS COPIED FROM Disposition_Offer__c.Broker__c, DELIBERATELY AND EXACTLY,
        MATCHING Broker_Assignment__c.Broker__c, BOV_Submission__c.Broker__c, Lease_Inquiry__c
        .Broker__c and Disposition__c.Broker__c. Same referenceTo, same ACTIVE non-optional
        lookupFilter, same errorMessage string, same deleteConstraint. There is no Broker__c
        OBJECT in this org; every "broker" in this application is a Contact on the
        Contact.Broker RECORD TYPE.

        🔴 DO NOT USE Contact.Is_Broker__c. That checkbox matches ZERO Contacts in this org -
        the broker definition moved to the Contact.Broker RECORD TYPE on 2026-08-20, and six
        fields were repointed off Is_Broker__c onto the record type that same day. This field
        follows that same, current definition from the start; it was never pointed at the
        retired checkbox.

        THIS FILTER IS ACTIVE AND NON-OPTIONAL, UNLIKE THE RETIRING Buyer__c FIELD IT REPLACES.
        Buyer__c's own comment explains at length why an active filter was wrong for a
        deal-scoped buyer principal with no seed population. That reasoning does not carry over:
        Broker__c targets the SAME durable, seeded population Disposition__c.Broker__c and
        Disposition_Offer__c.Broker__c already filter against - a real, non-empty Contact.Broker
        record-type population maintained by scripts/seed-broker-contacts.apex - so gating the
        picker on it costs nothing and prevents a non-broker Contact from ever being NDA'd.

        =====================================================================================
        LABEL: "Broker Contact", NOT "Broker". Matches Disposition_Offer__c.Broker__c,
        BOV_Submission__c.Broker__c and Disposition__c.Broker__c - every sibling Contact lookup
        on a deal-adjacent object in this repo uses this label. No field on NDA__c carries the
        bare label "Broker" today, so "Broker Contact" is unique here too and keeps this field
        consistent with its family rather than with the retiring Buyer__c ("Buyer Contact").

        =====================================================================================
        RELATIONSHIP NAME: Brokered_NDAs. COLLISION CHECKED, NOT ASSUMED.
        =====================================================================================
        Every referenceTo Contact field in this repo as of this change uses one of
        Broker_Assignments, Brokered_Dispositions, Lease_Inquiries, Brokered_Opportunities,
        Brokered_BOV_Submissions, Incoming_Broker_Changes, Outgoing_Broker_Changes, Buyer_NDAs
        (this object's own retiring field), Buyer_Disposition_Offers or
        Brokered_Disposition_Offers. Brokered_NDAs is free. The Brokered_ prefix matches
        Brokered_Dispositions/Brokered_Opportunities/Brokered_BOV_Submissions/
        Brokered_Disposition_Offers: under Contact, a bare "NDAs" would read as "this Contact's
        own NDAs" when the list actually means "NDAs this Contact BROKERS".
        ⚠ A relationshipName is disruptive to change after deploy. Settled here, before the
        first deploy, while it costs nothing.

        =====================================================================================
        🔴 NDA__c IS A DUAL-MODULE OBJECT. THIS FIELD IS INERT ON THE ACQUISITION SIDE.
        =====================================================================================
        NDA__c serves Acquisitions as well as Dispositions (both record types share this
        object). This field carries no record-type restriction and is technically settable on
        an acquisition NDA, but it is deliberately NOT added to any acquisition-specific
        permission set (DPEG_Acquisition_Edit / DPEG_Acquisition_View) or layout in this
        change - it ships FLS-invisible there, matching every other disposition-only field on
        this object (Buyer__c, Materials_Released_Date__c, Is_Disposition_NDA__c).

        deleteConstraint SetNull, matching every sibling Contact lookup in this repo - deleting
        a broker Contact must never delete the NDA that is evidence of what was sent or signed.

        =====================================================================================
        🔴 FLS: THIS FIELD IS INVISIBLE TO EVERYONE, ADMINS INCLUDED, UNTIL A PERMSET LANDS.
        =====================================================================================
        A Metadata API deployed custom field arrives with NO field permissions for any profile,
        System Administrator included. Read and edit are granted in DPEG_Disposition_Edit and
        read only in DPEG_Disposition_View in the same change - the two permission sets that
        already carried Buyer__c and carry every other NDA__c disposition-only field. Neither
        DPEG_Acquisition_Edit, DPEG_Acquisition_View nor DPEG_Admin_Access is touched (see the
        dual-module note above). This file and those two permission sets must deploy together.

        ⚠ TESTS MUST USE TestDataFactory.createBrokerContact / createBrokerContacts. The lookup
        filter below is ACTIVE and NOT optional - out of scope for this declarative change, but
        recorded here since it will bite the next Apex change that touches this field.
    -->
    <fullName>Broker__c</fullName>
    <deleteConstraint>SetNull</deleteConstraint>
    <description>The broker Contact this NDA is with - DPEG communicates only with the appointed listing broker on the sale, one per disposition. Replaces Buyer__c as the disposition NDA counterparty. Deliberately UNFILTERED on Acquisitions - see dual-module note in this file's comment.</description>
    <inlineHelpText>Pick the broker Contact this NDA is with. Only Contacts on the Broker record type can occupy this field.</inlineHelpText>
    <label>Broker Contact</label>
    <lookupFilter>
        <active>true</active>
        <booleanFilter>1</booleanFilter>
        <errorMessage>Only Broker Contacts can be selected here.</errorMessage>
        <filterItems>
            <field>Contact.RecordType.DeveloperName</field>
            <operation>equals</operation>
            <value>Broker</value>
        </filterItems>
        <isOptional>false</isOptional>
    </lookupFilter>
    <referenceTo>Contact</referenceTo>
    <relationshipLabel>Brokered NDAs</relationshipLabel>
    <relationshipName>Brokered_NDAs</relationshipName>
    <required>false</required>
    <trackHistory>false</trackHistory>
    <trackTrending>false</trackTrending>
    <type>Lookup</type>
</CustomField>
